      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{62df7cd83e007e467295c4e1|full_name}\n\nI checked and US English qwerty was the only option. Even on other language UI's. Imagine having korean, japanese, russian, and other languages that doesnt use the latin based english alphabet for UI, while keyboard is only qwerty English.\n\nWhich makes this issue harder for mutes that dont understand or cant write english.\n\nWhich means VRC needs a more diverse language options for keyboard. \n\nCopypasting isnt really fun.\n\nAnd it is possible to use 3rd party programs for a better translation which many does. Yet i dont really feel comfortable using a 3rd party program for such uses. And could be risky to use such too. And such programs have its disadvantages too.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
